# p1_locality.py seed=20261017

== A. semimeasure convention: cumulative loss in every order = -log nu(D) + log nu(empty) = -log nu(prove joint cell) + log nu(empty)
   226 instances, 1700 reveal orders; max |cumulative loss - (-log nu(D) + log nu(empty))| = 8.88e-16 bits

== B. normalised convention is not local and depends on the order
   G1 (else silent)   nu(empty)=1 nu(D)=1/2 | semimeasure loss 1.0000 bits | normalised loss -0.0000 bits
   G2 (else refutes)  nu(empty)=1 nu(D)=1/2 | semimeasure loss 1.0000 bits | normalised loss 1.0000 bits
   G3: semimeasure loss 2.0000 bits in both orders; normalised loss 2.0000 (a first) vs 1.5850 (weaker datum first)

== C. three-valued convention: cumulative loss = -log nu3(D) + log nu3(empty), every order
   259 (instance, order) pairs; three-valued conditionals sum to 1 at every step (asserted, exact); max deviation from telescoping 8.88e-16 bits

